  "speaker": "Abhinavagupta (devotee voice)",
  "question": "What if the self goes unscrutinized?",
  "premises": [
   "Unscrutinized self never shares thing-knowing; unscrutinized, without grasping-course, it is not.",
   "But Śiva — that self shining, one sap of all things — hence I, heart-devoted, ever blissful in Your hymn."
  ],
  "inference": "Unscrutinized, no knowing; scrutinized, Śiva shining one-sapped — bliss.",
  "uncertainties": [
   "'marśanavidhi elision kept; asau demonstrative force."
